Here's a solid folder structure for this system, based on the Django + DRF backend and React + Vite frontend described in your SRS. I'll explain the reasoning behind each part.

## Overall repo layout

```
attire-rental-system/
├── backend/                 # Django project
├── frontend/                # React project
├── docker-compose.yml        # Orchestrates backend, frontend, db, redis
├── .env.example
├── .gitignore
└── README.md
```

**Why separate top-level folders:** Your SRS specifies a decoupled client-server architecture (React frontend talking to a Django REST API). Keeping them as siblings (rather than nesting one inside the other) means each can have its own dependency management, Docker build, and CI pipeline without interfering with the other — and it maps directly to your two-container Docker Compose setup.

