## Infrastructure / root-level

```
attire-rental-system/
├── docker-compose.yml
│   services: backend, frontend, postgres, redis (optional), celery (optional)
├── nginx/                     # optional reverse proxy config for production
└── docs/
    ├── diagrams/               # Use case, sequence, activity diagrams from Section 4
    └── api-docs/               # OpenAPI/Swagger spec
```

**Why Docker Compose at the root:** Your architecture (Section 5.2) explicitly calls out Docker/Docker Compose as the infrastructure layer, coordinating Django, React, PostgreSQL, and optionally Redis/Celery (needed for FR8's async notification delivery) as one reproducible local/prod environment.

**Why a `docs/diagrams/` folder:** Section 4 references several diagrams (context, use case, activity, sequence) that should live versioned alongside the code rather than only in the SRS document, so they stay in sync as the system evolves.

